In article <28172022.14072@ics.uci.edu> wngai@southwark.ics.uci.edu (Wayne Ngai) writes:
] I like to know if there's anyway a casting a spell or use a wand on yourself?
	In addition to the directions 'h', 'j', 'k', 'l', and diagonals,
	there are also '>' (down), '<' (up), and '.' (right here).
	So if you're using something that wants a direction,
	you might try pointing it at yourself with '.'.

] Another thing, how do I go about gaining levels? 

	You gain experience points by killing things, though you can
	also gain levels by eating wraiths or quaffing gain-level potions.
	In your case, with three pet dragons killing anything before
	you get near it, it doesn't sound like you have much opportunity.
] What is the best way of raising my attributes?
] Potions and scrolls are hard to come by. 

	Hey, that's life in the big city.
	They do say that 'You are what you eat' - you might try
	eating various corpses and see what it does for you, if you
	can get anything before those pet dragons of yours do.

] I also, have a ring of conflict but I can't use it because
] my pet dragons would attack each other.  So any suggestions?  

	Well, this may not be very nice, but do you really NEED
	three pet dragons?  I know you can get really attached to
	the little guys, and they can be a lot of help if you're
	storming a castle or wiping out a room-ful of monsters,
	but face it, either you'll need to keep finding enough 
	Purina Dragon Chow for them or they'll start to get pretty hungry,
	and they might start thinking YOU look pretty good.
	And every time they kill something, they're gaining experience too -
	they get to be prety tough characters after a while.

] Should I just leave my 2 of my pet dragons behind on a level?

	I'll do that with dogs, since you can usually calm them down
	with a piece of tripe, but think for a while before you do
	that with dragons.  After all, you might want to come back
	there some day, and they'll get hungry if you leave them.
	It's a tough decision - the gods aren't real happy with 
	people who'd kill their own pet, but you might not be able
	to sneak past them.  That ring of conflict can come in handy,
	but hanging around a dragon-fight could be pretty electrifying.
	I'd probably go for it, and hope to have invisibility or
	teleport control when I came back to the level.

